{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe fish at Besseling’s table was tolerable, if a bit too white for my taste, and the Dutch wine was warm. I paid three guilders for the pleasure, which I find exorbitant for such a meal. Dr. Besseling is a pleasant enough Catholic, though he spoke of the Pope with a reverence I found rather theatrical. I have left Amsterdam for Utrecht by diligence, arriving as the light fails.\n\nI saw the former town hall here, now the imperial palace. It is a grand building, though one cannot help but feel a certain melancholy seeing the scars of Napoleon’s ambition still lingering on the walls. The coloured windows in the church were indeed striking; the light through them had a quality that almost made the stone feel alive. I am tired, my love. The journey has been long and the roads are not as smooth as one hopes. I hope the boys are well and that you have not had any trouble with the household accounts. I shall write again when I can find a quiet hour.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795218827,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":226,"prompt_tokens":1115,"total_tokens":1341,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-N7bbNEahL6i0PMj0DcGhviRmkQJ2UBsP","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1115,"prompt_ms":1101.783,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9881461883408071,"prompt_per_second":1011.9960101036231,"predicted_n":226,"predicted_ms":5338.892,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.72840888888889,"predicted_per_second":42.143575858061936}}